title AMUS4 — Constel exchange: two piers agree over frames alone
prompt Keaton set the recursion loop on the 1024-round itinerary and six-season double-seat: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, make progress before checking in, send often as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think AMUS3 (wire) landed and sent this turn — each handshake value crosses a frame whole and lawful. The AMUS3 road-on named AMUS4 as the two-party exchange loop. Lindy-first crux-first: this is the rung that turns three proven values and a proven frame into a proven conversation — the smallest whole a real transport (AMUS5 queue, AMUS6 socket) simply carries unchanged, so it is the durable contract, not a one-off.
think The crux beyond a function-call chain: the REAL pier boundary. Until now the handshake passed Zig values by pointer, as one program's locals. A real constellation has two piers, each holding only its own state and the bytes the other handed it. AMUS4 models exactly that — a Party is a pier's own view (name + claimed sky); the initiator never sees the responder's Ack value, only its frame, and the responder never sees the initiator's Greeting value, only its frame. exchange() reads the sealed Session back FROM the final frame, so even the completed value crossed the wire.
obs A red caught on metal: party() first ASSERTED membership (is_member), but a non-member is a legitimate NotAMember refusal path (test 4's xnz), so the assert panicked (reached unreachable). Fixed by refusing NotAMember by name at the earliest honest point — a pier must belong to the sky it claims — rather than asserting a caller-supplied fact. Reds-first: named it, closed it with the witness on metal, not a claim. The lesson: assert invariants the code establishes, refuse-by-name facts a caller supplies.
obs Witness proves on metal across five blocks: a clean exchange completes end to end across three frames (xnb and xnc agree over bytes alone); both sides read back the same sealed session; a mismatched sky refuses ConstellationMismatch mid-exchange (the greeting deframes fine, accept refuses); a non-member refuses NotAMember and a self-greet refuses SameParty; and a tampered greeting frame with a fixed-up digest refuses VowelPresent at the responder's border — the naming law guarding every crossing so a real-@p-shaped party cannot enter even over the wire. Witness GREEN, TAME bans clean, width exit 0; prior AMUS rungs stay GREEN (additive).
obs Kept docs synced in the same round (docs-implementation-sync): constel/README.md gains the exchange.rye rung, the run block lists amus_exchange_witness, Status and Kin weave include AMUS4, and the road-on now names AMUS5 (in-process byte queue) and AMUS6 (real Comlink socket) as the remaining seam.
loom witness=amus_exchange_witness blocks=5 frames_per_exchange=3 wall_ms_note=selftest under a second after build
